+##### onRetry(context)
+
+Type: `Function`
+
+Callback invoked only when another attempt is going to happen, right before the wait. Receives the same context object as `onFailedAttempt`. Unlike `onFailedAttempt`, it is not called for the final failure, which makes it suited to counting retries.
+
+The function is called _after_ `onFailedAttempt`, `shouldConsumeRetry`, and `shouldRetry`. It is _not_ called when the error is rethrown: on `AbortError`, on an abort through `signal`, on a `TypeError` (except network errors), when `shouldRetry` returns `false`, or when `retries` or `maxRetryTime` are exhausted.
+
+The function can return a promise, which is awaited before the wait starts. If it throws, all retries will be aborted and the original promise will reject with the thrown error.
+
+```js
+import pRetry from 'p-retry';
+
+const run = async () => { … };
+
+const result = await pRetry(run, {
+	onRetry: ({error, attemptNumber, retryDelay}) => {
+		metrics.increment('retries');
+	}
+});
+```
+
 ##### shouldRetry(context)
 
 Type: `Function`
